## 🚀 Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Node.js
- npm

### Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/urosv2/Miamaya-Cypress-Automated-Testing.git
```

Navigate to the project:

```bash
cd Miamaya-Cypress-Automated-Testing
```

Install dependencies:

```bash
npm install
```

### Running Tests

Open Cypress Test Runner:

```bash
npx cypress open
```

Run all tests in headless mode:

```bash
npx cypress run
```

Run a specific test file:

```bash
npx cypress run --spec "cypress/e2e/example.cy.js"
```

Replace the example path with an existing test file.

## 📁 Project Structure

A typical Cypress project is organized as follows:

```text
cypress/
├── e2e/          # Automated test specifications
├── fixtures/     # Test data
└── support/      # Shared commands and configuration
cypress.config.js
package.json
README.md
```

The exact structure depends on the project configuration.

